  <data name="FirstRunWelcomeTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Welcome to Battery Care Portal</value></data>
  <data name="FirstRunWelcomeText" xml:space="preserve"><value>This app keeps your laptop battery healthy. It can hold the charge at a lower level, remind you when to unplug, and show how the battery is doing. Nothing is changed until you choose it, and you can skip any step.</value></data>
  <data name="FirstRunCheckTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Your laptop</value></data>
  <data name="FirstRunChecking" xml:space="preserve"><value>Checking what your laptop supports. Nothing is changed.</value></data>
  <data name="FirstRunActionOfferChargeLimit" xml:space="preserve"><value>Good news: the charge limit works on this laptop. The next step lets you turn it on.</value></data>
  <data name="FirstRunActionPowerPlanManagerOwnsCharging" xml:space="preserve"><value>The charge limit works on this laptop, but Power Plan Manager is already handling charging. Only one app should set the limit, so this app leaves it to Power Plan Manager.</value></data>
  <data name="FirstRunActionInstallMakerDriver" xml:space="preserve"><value>One step is missing: the maker&apos;s battery software or driver was not found. Install it from your laptop maker or Windows Update, then use Check again on the Overview page. Until then the app shows your battery and sends reminders.</value></data>
  <data name="FirstRunActionConsiderBetaTesting" xml:space="preserve"><value>Your laptop is on our test list, so the charge limit stays off for now. You can help test it in Settings. Until then the app shows your battery and sends reminders.</value></data>
  <data name="FirstRunActionUseReminders" xml:space="preserve"><value>This laptop has no charge limit the app can use. It will show your battery and remind you to unplug.</value></data>
  <data name="FirstRunActionNothingToDo" xml:space="preserve"><value>No battery was found, so there is nothing to look after on this device.</value></data>
  <data name="FirstRunLimitTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Turn on the charge limit?</value></data>
  <data name="FirstRunLimitText" xml:space="preserve"><value>The laptop keeps the limit by itself, even when this app is closed. You can top up to 100% any time, and Restore laptop defaults is always available. Windows may ask for permission.</value></data>
  <data name="FirstRunLimitTurnOn" xml:space="preserve"><value>Turn on the charge limit</value></data>
